---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy | Calan" description="How Calan handles information submitted through this website." pageClass="legal-page">
  <header class="legal-header shell">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">Calan</a>
    <a href="/">Back to home</a>
  </header>
  <main class="shell">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <article class="legal-content">
      <p>Last updated September 26, 2026</p>

      <h2>About this notice</h2>
      <p>
        This notice describes the information collected through the Calan marketing website and waitlist.
        It does not yet describe the Calan application, which will have a separate privacy notice before launch.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        If you join the waitlist, we collect the email address you provide. Cloudflare may also process
        limited technical information, such as an IP address and browser details, to deliver the website
        and protect the form from abuse. We do not sell your personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email address to manage the waitlist and send occasional product, availability, and
        early-access updates about Calan. You can unsubscribe from those messages at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage and service providers</h2>
      <p>
        Waitlist addresses are stored using Cloudflare D1. Cloudflare provides website hosting, database,
        and abuse-prevention services and processes related technical data on our behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask us to remove your email address from the waitlist. Contact details for privacy requests
        will be added before the public launch. Until then, every waitlist email will include an unsubscribe option.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this notice as Calan develops. The date at the top of this page indicates the latest revision.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
